    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence).\n\n**`CustomerCodeGenerator`** \u2014 the formatting unit:\n- `generate(city, lastName, sequence)` now emits `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n- Extracted a small private `prefix(value)` helper (upper-case, first three chars) so the city and last-name prefixes are derived by one shared rule instead of duplicated logic.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 the wiring:\n- The sequence is now *per-city*: `countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) + 1`, matching \"one more than the owners already in that city.\"\n- Added a focused `countOwnersInCity(city)` helper (case-insensitive), mirroring the existing `countNamesakes` style and reusing the existing `equalsIgnoreCase` helper.\n\n**`MembershipNumberGenerator`** \u2014 no change needed: it already builds the membership number from `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it's automatically rebuilt on the new format. That's the only value derived from the customer code.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
